/-!
# Two movers, frozen readings [1, 2, 3], one mover at or below 1: a lonely instant for ALL such pairs (GENERATED by `s2below_gen_v1.py`)

Written 2026-10-23.  New file.  Lonely pieces of the frozen set in one lap (period 1, exact): [1/8, 7/24], [3/8, 7/16], [9/16, 5/8], [17/24, 7/8].
* `small123` (`0 < d1 ≤ 1/8`, `d1 ≤ d2`, no other bound): `d2 ≥ 2` by `small_A` on the widest piece `[1/8, 7/24]`; `d2 < 2` and `distInt d2 ≥ d1/2` by `small_II` at the frozen-clear
  point `1/8`; `d2 < 2` within `d1/2` of an integer `j ∈ [1, 2]` by `small_I_pos` / `small_I_neg` at a frozen-clear point `τ0` with `j τ0` in the window (patterns below).
  Patterns (j, sign: τ0, N): (1,+: 1/4, 0); (1,-: 1/4, 0); (2,+: 1/4, 0); (2,-: 1/4, 0).
* `col123_<i>` (`1/8 ≤ d1 ≤ 1`): finite box cover of `{d1 ≤ d2}`, `3` columns in `d1`, `8` boxes, kinds {'P': 5, 'R1a': 3}, pieces up to lap 1 (lap-shifted copies of the frozen pieces;
  `ex_of_piece`).  [PROVISIONAL: covering]; `r1_rect` is [PROVISIONAL: counting tool].
* `exists_below_123`: for ALL `0 < d1 ≤ 1`, `d1 ≤ d2`: `∃ t > 0, FClear F t ∧ Clear2 d1 d2 t`.
